text.section:
The clerk shall assess, in addition to the fees provided for by § 17.1-275.1, 17.1-275.2, 17.1-275.3, 17.1-275.4, 17.1-275.7, 17.1-275.8, 17.1-275.9, 17.1-275.10, 17.1-275.11, 17.1-275.11:1, or 17.1-275.12, the following costs:

Any amount paid by the Commonwealth for legal representation of the defendant;


Any amount paid for trial transcripts;


Extradition costs;


Costs of psychiatric evaluation;


Costs taxed against the defendant as appellant under Rule 5A:30 of the Rules of the Supreme Court;


Any fee for a returned check or disallowed credit card charge assessed pursuant to subdivision A 28 of § 17.1-275;


Any jury costs;


Any assessment made pursuant to subdivision A 10 of § 17.1-275;


Any fees prescribed in §§ 18.2-268.8 and 46.2-341.26:8;


Any court costs related to an ignition interlock device;


Any fee for testing for HIV;


Any fee for processing an individual admitted to jail as prescribed in § 15.2-1613.1;


Any fee for courthouse security personnel as prescribed in § 53.1-120;


Any fee for a DNA sample as prescribed in § 19.2-310.2;


Reimbursement to the Commonwealth of medical fees as prescribed in § 19.2-165.1;


Any fee for a local criminal justice training academy as prescribed in § 9.1-106;


Any fee prescribed by §§ 16.1-69.48:1.01 and 17.1-275.11;


Any expenses charged pursuant to subsection B or F of § 19.2-187.1; and


Any fee for an electronic summons system as prescribed in § 17.1-279.1.
